@startuml
title ATM Withdrawal State Transition Diagram

state "Initial" as InitialState
InitialState : entry / User approaches ATM
InitialState : do / Ready for transaction
InitialState : exit / Waiting for user action

state "Select Amount" as SelectAmount
SelectAmount : entry / Display predefined options and custom input
SelectAmount : do / Choose predefined or enter custom amount
SelectAmount : exit / Selected an amount or decided to cancel

state "Predefined Selection" as PredefinedSelection
PredefinedSelection : entry / User selects predefined amount
PredefinedSelection : do / Capture selected amount
PredefinedSelection : exit / Proceed to processing

state "Custom Amount Entry" as CustomEntry
CustomEntry : entry / User chooses custom input
CustomEntry : do / Enter and validate custom amount
CustomEntry : exit / Proceed to processing

state "Processing Withdrawal" as Processing
Processing : entry / System processes withdrawal request
Processing : do / Deduct funds and dispense cash
Processing : exit / Transaction complete or error occurs

state "Cancel Transaction" as CancelTransaction
CancelTransaction : entry / User decides to cancel
CancelTransaction : do / Abort transaction
CancelTransaction : exit / Return card to user

state J0 <<choice>>
state Merge1 <<merge>>

InitialState --> SelectAmount : [User selects amount option]

SelectAmount --> PredefinedSelection : [Predefined amount selected]
SelectAmount --> CustomEntry : [Custom amount chosen]
SelectAmount --> CancelTransaction : [User cancels transaction]

PredefinedSelection --> Processing
CustomEntry --> Processing

Processing --> [*] : [Withdrawal successful]
Processing --> CancelTransaction : [Error occurs or user cancels]

CancelTransaction --> InitialState : [Return card and exit]

InitialState --> Merge1 : [Any point during processing]
Merge1 --> [*] : [User returns without completing transaction]
@enduml
